      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To dry out the area, you can use compressed air or a soft-bristled brush to gently remove any moisture or debris. Avoid using a vacuum cleaner or sucking up any moisture, as this can push dirt further in. As for determining whether the leak sensor is faulty or a temporary issue, look for a water level marker on the sensor; if it's low or incorrect, it may be a sign of a faulty sensor. If the water level indicator is normal, but you're still experiencing a leak, the sensor might be working, and the leak may be caused by another component or issue.",
